// MIDI "Drums" mode workflow.
// id = "drums" → workflow id "midi-drums" (matches the basename here).
//
// Activated by the FTS_MIDI_MODE_DRUMS action (or the midi-mode bridge).
// Inline bindings below auto-create the overlay "workflow-midi-drums" and
// only apply while a MIDI editor is focused (context @Midi).
//
// The MIDI-editor *view* setup for drums (drum-map note names, triangle
// note view, etc.) is applied in Rust (fts-extensions `midi_mode_input`)
// because it must run in the MIDI Editor section, which the workflow
// `settings(...)` block (main section) can't reach.

name        "Drums"
description "Drum programming: drum-map view + drum keybinds."

bindings (
    // `passthrough true`: this is a main-section FTS extension action that
    // targets the MIDI editor itself, so it must run in the main section even
    // though it's only active while the MIDI editor is focused (context @Midi).
    {keys f, action FTS_MIDI_INSERT_FLAM, context @Midi, passthrough true, desc "Insert flam at mouse cursor"}
)
